# direnv: load .env into the shell environment when you enter this directory.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS (hikari's .envrc the precedent — the same cure for the same
# wrapper class): opencode has no native .env loader, and the web tool reads
# TAVILY_API_KEY / CONTEXT7_API_KEY from process.env at call time — process env
# is fixed at session LAUNCH, so the keys must already be in the shell that
# launches opencode. direnv + this file does that.
#
# NO SECRETS LIVE HERE — only in .env (which is gitignored). This file just tells
# direnv to load that .env. Safe to commit.
#
# SETUP (once per machine):
#   1. brew install direnv          # already installed on this machine
#   2. Add to ~/.zshrc:  eval "$(direnv hook zsh)"
#   3. Restart shell, then run:  direnv allow
dotenv
